(*
A non-literal block (held in a temp, not inlined by the compiler) invoked via
`value:`. This is the case that today routes through the dispatch.c
BytecodeClosureVtable intercept and, after the OP_BLOCK_INVOKE task, routes
through the new opcode instead — value-family sends on a receiver that IS a
closure.

expect:
42
*)
class BlockInvokeTest packageUsing: manifest = () (
public main: platform args: args = (
    | adder result |
    adder:: [:x | x + 1].
    result:: adder value: 41.
    result printString out.
)
) : (
)
